    "thm-nrqmx-adiabatic-geometric-phase-bound": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-countable-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Countable Choice**, written $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, is the following\nstatement.\n\n> For every family $(X_n)_{n \\in \\mathbb{N}}$ of nonempty sets indexed by\n> $\\mathbb{N}$ there is a function $f$ with domain $\\mathbb{N}$ such that\n> $f(n) \\in X_n$ for every $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$.\n\nEquivalently, in the vocabulary of Choice function: every at most\ncountable family of nonempty sets has a choice function.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-nrqm-controlled-dynamics-finite-gapped-adiabatic-estimate",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let\n$H:[0,1]\\to\\operatorname{Herm}(\\mathbb C^d)$ be a map of class $C^2$ into the\nHermitian $d\\times d$ matrices, let $P(s)$ be the spectral projection of $H(s)$\nfor a spectral cluster $\\sigma_P(s)$ that is separated from the complementary\nspectrum by a uniform gap: $\\operatorname{dist}(\\sigma_P(s),\\sigma(H(s))\\setminus\\sigma_P(s))\\ge g>0$\nfor all $s\\in[0,1]$. Require that the cluster is followed coherently:\n$P(s)$ is continuous in operator norm (equivalently, it follows the local\nRiesz continuation of its initial cluster). Fix $T>0$. Let $U_T$ solve\n$i\\,\\partial_sU_T(s)=TH(s)U_T(s)$, $U_T(0)=I$\nby the finite matrix construction below, and let\n$U_A$ solve $i\\,\\partial_sU_A(s)=\\bigl(TH(s)+i[P'(s),P(s)]\\bigr)U_A(s)$,\n$U_A(0)=I$ (equivalently $U_A'=(-iTH+K)U_A$ with $K=[P',P]$). Then:\n\n(a) $P\\in C^2([0,1];\\operatorname{End}(\\mathbb C^d))$ and $K=[P',P]$ is\nanti-Hermitian of class $C^1$ with $[K,P]=P'$.\n\n(b) There is a $C^1$ Hermitian $X:[0,1]\\to\\operatorname{End}(\\mathbb C^d)$ with\n$[H(s),X(s)]=K(s)$ for all $s$.\n\n(c) *Intertwining.* $P(s)U_A(s)=U_A(s)P(0)$ for all $s$.\n\n(d) *Adiabatic estimate.* With\n$C:=2\\sup_s\\|X(s)\\|+\\int_0^1\\bigl(\\|X'(s)\\|+\\|K(s)\\|\\|X(s)\\|\\bigr)ds$ one has\n$$\\bigl\\|(I-P(s))U_T(s)P(0)\\bigr\\|\\le\\frac CT\\qquad(s\\in[0,1]).$$\n\nThe estimate is finite-dimensional and conditional on the uniform positive gap;\ngap-closing families and unbounded families are not covered.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-nrqmx-berry-projector-curvature",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $M$, $d$, and $P$ satisfy [[def-nrqmx-smooth-projector-bundle]], with constant rank $r$. The curvature of the projected connection $\\nabla=P\\,d$, as an endomorphism-valued two-form on $\\mathbb C^d$, is\n$$F=P(dP\\wedge dP)P.$$\nFor any local $C^2$ orthonormal frame $V:U\\to\\mathbb C^{d\\times r}$ with $V^*V=I_r$ and $P=VV^*$, its connection matrix $A=V^*dV$ is anti-Hermitian and its curvature matrix is $F_{\\mathrm{fr}}=dA+A\\wedge A=V^*FV$. If $V'=Vg$ for a $C^2$ map $g:U\\to U(r)$, then $A'=g^{-1}Ag+g^{-1}dg$ and $F'_{\\mathrm{fr}}=g^{-1}F_{\\mathrm{fr}}g$. Along every $C^2$ path, Kato transport is unitary and intertwines the endpoint projectors.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "supplier_excerpts": [
