          "consumer_use": "[F2] [F2] [[thm-nrqmx-berry-projector-curvature]]: the Kato generator is $K=[P',P]$, and its transport satisfies $P(s)W(s)=W(s)P(0)$."
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Divide the evolution equation by $\\hbar$ and set $\\tau=T/\\hbar>0$. Then $i\\,\\partial_sU_T=\\tau H(s)U_T$, exactly the scale convention of [F1], with the same $H$, $P$, $K$, and $X$. The supplier's hypotheses hold: $H$ is $C^2$, the cluster is coherently followed, and its complementary spectral distance is uniformly at least $g>0$. Therefore its estimate gives $\\|(I-P(s))U_T(s)P(0)\\|\\leq C/\\tau=\\hbar C/T$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "A1",
            "F1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Suppose $\\operatorname{rank}P=1$ and $HP=EP$. By [F2], $W'=KW$, $P(s)W(s)=W(s)P(0)$, and $W$ is unitary. Set $V(s)=W(s)\\exp(-i\\tau\\int_0^sE(u)\\,du)$. For $v\\in\\operatorname{ran}P(0)$, intertwining gives $W(s)v\\in\\operatorname{ran}P(s)$, so $H(s)W(s)v=E(s)W(s)v$. Differentiating therefore gives $V'(s)v=(-i\\tau H(s)+K(s))V(s)v$, with $V(0)v=v$. The defined $U_A$ satisfies the same matrix initial-value equation $U_A'=(-i\\tau H+K)U_A$; uniqueness of finite-dimensional linear ODE solutions yields $U_A(s)v=V(s)v$ for every such $v$, which is the stated factorization.",
