          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\\geq1$, let $H\\in C^2([0,1],\\operatorname{Herm}(\\mathbb C^d))$ be a finite Hermitian family with energy unit joules, and let $\\hbar>0$ have unit joule-seconds. A spectral cluster at $s$ is a subset $\\sigma_P(s)$ of the finite spectrum of $H(s)$, and $P(s)$ is the orthogonal projection onto the sum of its eigenspaces. Coherently followed means that $s\\mapsto P(s)$ is continuous in operator norm (equivalently, it agrees locally with the Riesz continuation of its initial cluster). Assume the distance from $\\sigma_P(s)$ to the complementary spectrum is at least a uniform $g>0$ in joules. Let $T>0$ be a total duration in seconds, let $s=t/T$ be dimensionless, and let $U_T(0)=I$ solve\n$$i\\hbar\\,\\partial_sU_T(s)=T H(s)U_T(s).$$\nPut $K(s)=[P'(s),P(s)]$. There is a $C^1$ Hermitian matrix $X(s)$ solving $[H(s),X(s)]=K(s)$. With\n$$C=2\\sup_{s\\in[0,1]}\\|X(s)\\|+\\int_0^1\\bigl(\\|X'(s)\\|+\\|K(s)\\|\\,\\|X(s)\\|\\bigr)\\,ds,$$\nthe leakage satisfies\n$$\\|(I-P(s))U_T(s)P(0)\\|\\leq\\frac{\\hbar C}{T}\\qquad(0\\leq s\\leq1).$$\nThe supplier provides a $C^1$ Hermitian $X$ solving the displayed commutator equation. For that $X$, $C$ has unit joule-inverse, so $\\hbar C/T$ is dimensionless. If the cluster has rank one, with $H(s)P(s)=E(s)P(s)$, define $U_A(0)=I$ by\n$$i\\,\\partial_sU_A(s)=\\left(\\frac{T}{\\hbar}H(s)+iK(s)\\right)U_A(s).$$\nFor Kato transport $W'(s)=K(s)W(s)$, $W(0)=I$, the comparison evolution factors exactly on the initial eigenspace:\n$$U_A(s)P(0)=\\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{iT}{\\hbar}\\int_0^sE(u)\\,du\\right)W(s)P(0).$$\nThe leakage estimate is finite-dimensional and conditional on the stated uniform positive gap.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[A1] [A1] Countable Choice is [[def-countable-choice]], the hypothesis carried by [[thm-nrqmx-adiabatic-geometric-phase-bound]].\n\n[F1] [F1] [[thm-nrqmx-adiabatic-geometric-phase-bound]]: the $O(1/T)$ leakage conclusion requires a coherently followed spectral projection separated from the complementary spectrum by a uniform positive gap.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Current Step 1 draft; complete current proof inspected; independent acceptance is not inferred.",
          "consumer_use": "[A1] [A1] Countable Choice is [[def-countable-choice]], the hypothesis carried by [[thm-nrqmx-adiabatic-geometric-phase-bound]].\n\n[F1] [F1] [[thm-nrqmx-adiabatic-geometric-phase-bound]]: the $O(1/T)$ leakage conclusion requires a coherently followed spectral projection separated from the complementary spectrum by a uniform positive gap."
        }
