      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "On $\\mathbb C^2$, let $e_\\uparrow=(1,0)^T$, $e_\\downarrow=(0,1)^T$, and $H(s)=E_0s\\,\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1)$ for $s\\in[-1,1]$. For $s<0$ the ordered upper eigenvalue is $-E_0s$ and its projection is $P_{\\rm up}(s)=e_\\downarrow e_\\downarrow^*$; for $s>0$ it is $E_0s$ and its projection is $P_{\\rm up}(s)=e_\\uparrow e_\\uparrow^*$. At $s=0$ the only spectral projection is $I_2$, so no continuous rank-one extension of the ordered upper projection exists. The gap between the two eigenvalues is $2E_0|s|$, which closes at zero.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "A1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "The propagator from $s=-1$ solves $i\\hbar U_T'(s)=T H(s)U_T(s)$ and is\n$$U_T(s)=\\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{iTE_0}{2\\hbar}(s^2-1)\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1)\\right),$$\nas direct differentiation verifies. In particular $U_T(1)=I_2$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "step 1.1",
            "construct",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "At the endpoints, $P_{\\rm up}(-1)=e_\\downarrow e_\\downarrow^*$ and $P_{\\rm up}(1)=e_\\uparrow e_\\uparrow^*$. Therefore\n$$\\bigl\\|(I-P_{\\rm up}(1))U_T(1)P_{\\rm up}(-1)\\bigr\\|=\\|e_\\downarrow e_\\downarrow^*\\|=1$$\nfor every $T>0$. No finite constant $C$ independent of $T$ can bound this leakage by $C/T$. The ordered projection fails the continuity and uniform-gap hypotheses in [F1].",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "step 1.1",
            "step 2.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-4-1",
          "claim": "The constant projection $P_\\downarrow=e_\\downarrow e_\\downarrow^*$ is instead a continuous spectral projection through the crossing, commutes with every $H(s)$, and has zero leakage for all $T$. Thus the example refutes a gap-free uniform tracking claim for the ordered branch; it does not assert that every branch crossing causes transitions.",
          "step": "4.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "step 1.1",
            "step 2.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "finite_checks": [
