          "status": "Published mathematical supplier; exact current Statement inspected.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $M$ be an oriented smooth $n$-manifold with boundary, $n\\geq1$, and let $\\eta\\in\\Omega_c^{n-1}(M)$. With $j:\\partial M\\hookrightarrow M$ and the outward-normal-first orientation,\n$$\\int_M d\\eta=\\int_{\\partial M}j^*\\eta.$$\nAn empty boundary contributes zero; in dimension one its integral is a finite signed sum of point values.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F4] [F4] [[thm-general-stokes-theorem]]: under Countable Choice, for a smooth real one-form on a compact oriented smooth surface region with smooth boundary, the exterior-derivative integral equals the outward-normal-first boundary integral.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Published result; complete current Statement and proof inspected for the scoped use.",
          "consumer_use": "[F4] [F4] [[thm-general-stokes-theorem]]: under Countable Choice, for a smooth real one-form on a compact oriented smooth surface region with smooth boundary, the exterior-derivative integral equals the outward-normal-first boundary integral."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "thm-multidimensional-integral-properties",
          "carrier": "items/thm-multidimensional-integral-properties.md",
          "status": "Published mathematical supplier; exact current Statement inspected.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $Q=\\prod_{j<m}[a_j,b_j]$ be nondegenerate. For integrable\n$f,g:Q\\to\\mathbb R$ and scalars $\\alpha,\\beta$, the function\n$\\alpha f+\\beta g$ is integrable and its integral is\n$\\alpha\\int_Qf+\\beta\\int_Qg$. If $f\\le g$, then\n$\\int_Qf\\le\\int_Qg$. Also $|f|$ is integrable and\n$|\\int_Qf|\\le\\int_Q|f|$. If $a_r<c<b_r$, cutting $Q$ at the coordinate\nhyperplane $x_r=c$ gives two nondegenerate subrectangles; integrability on\n$Q$ is equivalent to integrability on both restrictions, and their integral\nvalues add to the integral over $Q$.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F5] [F5] [[thm-multidimensional-integral-properties]]: coordinate integrals are linear, obey monotonicity, and satisfy $|\\int f|\\leq\\int|f|$; hence uniform convergence of continuous coefficients on a compact coordinate region implies convergence of their integrals.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Published result; complete current Statement and proof inspected for the scoped use.",
          "consumer_use": "[F5] [F5] [[thm-multidimensional-integral-properties]]: coordinate integrals are linear, obey monotonicity, and satisfy $|\\int f|\\leq\\int|f|$; hence uniform convergence of continuous coefficients on a compact coordinate region implies convergence of their integrals."
