            "construct",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "The projector $P_+\\circ g$ is $C^2$ and rank one. Its projected curvature is $g^*F_+$: applying [F1] to $P_+\\circ g$, the chain rule and [F4] give $d(P_+\\circ g)=g^*dP_+$ and preserve the ordered wedge product. Thus [F2] gives\n$$-\\frac1{4\\pi}\\left(\\int_{D^2}f_0^*\\omega-\\int_{D^2}f_1^*\\omega\\right)=\\frac{i}{2\\pi}\\int\\operatorname{tr}F_{P_+\\circ g}\\in\\mathbb Z,$$\nwhere the coefficient is $-1/(4\\pi)$ because $i\\cdot i=-1$. Rearranging proves the stated $4\\pi$ period. This is a topological ambiguity statement for the same boundary loop; no physical observation is involved.",
